<h2>Segment 223 &mdash; three proposed ways to retain karma</h2>
<div class="pair">
<div class="tib"><div class="lab">TIBETAN (WYLIE)</div>
<span class="u" data-d="1" data-l="s223S"><span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s223w1">las</span> <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s223w2">byas</span> pa&#x27;i <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s223w3">skad cig</span> gnyis par &#x27;gags zin pa&#x27;i snga logs kyi <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s223w4">las</span> <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s223w5">&#x27;gag pa</span> la <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s223w6">mngon du phyogs pa</span>&#x27;i tshe, <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s223w7">las</span> kyi <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s223w8">nus pa</span> <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s223w9">gzhag</span> par bya ba&#x27;i <span class="u" data-d="6" data-l="s223w10">phyir</span> <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s223w11">kha cig</span> <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s223w12">kun gzhi <span class="u" data-d="7" data-l="s223w13">rnam par shes pa</span></span> <span class="u" data-d="3" data-l="s223w14">rtog par byed</span> la, <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s223w15">kha cig</span> <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s223w16">bu lon</span> gyi dpang rgya ste de&#x27;i <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s223w17">yi ge</span> dang <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s223w18">&#x27;dra ba</span>&#x27;i <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s223w19">las</span> <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s223w20">gnyis</span> las <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s223w21">don gzhan</span> pa, <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s223w22">chud mi za ba</span> <span class="u" data-d="3" data-l="s223w23">zhes pa</span> <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s223w24">ldan min <span class="u" data-d="7" data-l="s223w25">&#x27;du byed</span></span> du gyur pa cig <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s223w26">&#x27;dod</span> do, , <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s223w27">kha cig</span> ni <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s223w28">las</span> <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s223w29">gnyis</span> kyi <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s223w30">thob pa</span> <span class="u" data-d="3" data-l="s223w31">zhes pa</span> de gnyis las <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s223w32">don gzhan</span> du gyur pa&#x27;i <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s223w33">ldan min</span> zhig <span class="u" data-d="3" data-l="s223w34">rtog par byed</span> do</span>
</div>
<div class="eng"><div class="lab">GESHE MICHAEL'S ENGLISH (VERBATIM)</div>
<span class="u" data-d="1" data-l="s223S">Let&#x27;s consider the <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s223w1">deed or karma</span> as it exists up to the point right after the <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s223w3">moment</span> in which the deed is <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s223w2">completed</span>; that is, let&#x27;s consider the <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s223w4">deed</span> as it <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s223w6">approaches</span> its <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s223w5">end</span>. The <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s223w8">energy</span> of the <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s223w7">deed</span> has to be <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s223w9">stored</span> somewhere, and <span class="u" data-d="6" data-l="s223w10">so</span> <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s223w11">some</span> thinkers have <span class="u" data-d="3" data-l="s223w14">invented</span> the idea of some kind of <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s223w12">foundation <span class="u" data-d="7" data-l="s223w13">consciousness</span></span> for it to stay. <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s223w15">Others</span> have <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s223w26">said</span> that there is something which is <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s223w24"><span class="u" data-d="7" data-l="s223w25">changing</span> but neither mental nor physical</span>, something they <span class="u" data-d="3" data-l="s223w23">call</span> &quot;the <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s223w22">fact of not just going away</span>&quot;; they say it is something that exists <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s223w21">separately</span> from the <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s223w20">two</span> types of <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s223w19">deeds</span> [virtue and non-virtue], and that it <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s223w18">resembles</span> the <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s223w17">document</span> written up for a <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s223w16">loan that has to be repaid</span>. Still <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s223w27">others</span> have <span class="u" data-d="3" data-l="s223w34">invented</span> the idea that there is another changing thing which is <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s223w33">neither mental nor physical</span>, again <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s223w32">different</span> from the <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s223w29">two</span> kinds of <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s223w28">deeds</span> themselves, something they <span class="u" data-d="3" data-l="s223w31">call</span> a &quot;<span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s223w30">hold</span>.&quot;</span>
</div>
</div>
<div class="note"><b>AI NOTE</b> &mdash; Provisional machine alignment by Codex, independent Tibetan-first proposal. The opening temporal construction is freely recast: gnyis par and the cessation/prior-time wording are omitted rather than assigned to misleading English atoms. Only the clearly recoverable deed/completed/moment/end/approaches words are aligned. The first las owns deed or karma; the repeated English deed within the completion relative clause is unwrapped. gzhag → stored is a contextual corpus match, not adoption of its unrelated provisional glossary gloss. dpang rgya and written up remain unwrapped because the document formulation distributes the explanatory dpang rgya ste de'i yi ge phrase. chud mi za ba and ldan min 'du byed are established technical compounds; their English articles and supplied participants stay unwrapped. The final ldan min owns only neither mental nor physical. The two occurrences of rtog par byed and zhes pa are phrase mappings at depth 3. C16:800 agrees in all three compared text fields; no independent publication or ingestion lineage is inferred.</div>
